Here are the concrete bugs and design problems found in the provided code, ordered by severity.

### 1. Critical: Incorrect Model Path Loading in `common_speculative_init_result`
**File:** `speculative.cpp` (implied)
**Function:** `common_speculative_init_result::common_speculative_init_result`

**Bug:** When loading a separate draft model (non-MTP case), the code loads the model from the **target** model's path instead of the **draft** model's path.

```cpp
// Line ~1450 in the provided snippet
if (has_draft) {
    model_path = params.speculative.draft.mparams.path; // Correct path stored in variable
    LOG_INF("%s: loading draft model '%s'\n", __func__, model_path.c_str());
    // ...
    // BUG: Uses params.model.path (Target Model Path) instead of model_path (Draft Model Path)
    llama_model * model_dft = llama_model_load_from_file(params.model.path.c_str(), mparams); 
    // ...
}
```
**Impact:** The server will attempt to load the large target model as the draft model. This will likely fail due to memory constraints
